{
  "quest.4F33BBD62C89D3D1.title": "&6Heart of Luna",
  "quest.7246368D781AF664.title": "&3Gravity Manipulator",
  "quest.751C9ACFF61D9B4A.title": "&aOxygen Module",
  "quest.2AB8372D4923EB79.title": "&6Launch Pad Towers",
  "quest.48793376ABF73D9D.title": "&6Rocket Parts",
  "quest.7E33FAE9B28F310C.quest_desc": [
    "Titanium tools have 3122 durability and 9.6 mining speed, more than diamond tools on both counts, and they harvest everything a diamond pickaxe can.",
    "",
    "The set includes a sword as well. They are worth making if you expect to spend much time underground looking for more titanium.",
  ],
  "quest.353A4A8D9B1F1535.title": "&aDamage Protection",
  "quest.1FD2A6DDDD6FC1DC.title": "&aBlender",
  "quest.6B965F82617C0CBB.title": "&3Oil Finder",
  "quest.7E33FAE9B28F310C.title": "&aTitanium Tools",
  "quest.050D217525CEB718.title": "&3Cargo Unloader",
  "quest.29B8507F3604F167.title": "&3Antenna",
  "quest.381894100844F900.title": "&3Space Farm",
  "quest.4FE1E26A7C5491C4.title": "&bThe Tablet",
  "quest.115BB85719D018FA.quest_desc": [
    "Stores 16000 FE and can work as a buffer without any special setup. It takes power when your generators produce more than you need and supplies it again when demand rises.",
    "",
    "Put a &aSpace Suit Helmet&r in the output slot to charge the battery used by its night vision and oil finder modules.",
    "",
    "&7&oIt keeps its charge when broken, making it easy to carry a full one between bases.&r",
  ],
  "quest.21619170E62020C5.title": "&3Fuel Refinery",
  "quest.7908A372EC4E1475.title": "&dLaboratory",
  "quest.4F33BBD62C89D3D1.quest_desc": [
    "&zThe Heart of Luna&r waits at the bottom of the deep lab. It has 550 health and deals 14 damage, and it barely needs to move to be dangerous.",
    "",
    "Twice during the fight it becomes invulnerable until it finishes its response. Attacks during those phases deal no damage.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It guards the direction it is facing. Attacks from the front are deflected and leave it guarded for several seconds, but it cannot defend against attacks from behind.",
    "",
    "When it roars, its damage doubles for 15 seconds and it leaves behind a cloud that infects anything caught in it. &cThe ray is the real danger.&r A shield can absorb most of its damage.",
  ],
  "quest.6DA7B8D6730BA6E5.quest_desc": [
    "&3Memory Chips&r left behind by the missions that came before you. Read them in order to learn what happened on the Moon.",
    "",
    "Find them in satellite and operation-base chests on Earth, in meteors, and in Moon villages, spheres, dungeons and abandoned space stations. Research also rewards them.",
    "",
    "Read them on the &bTablet&r. A blank card that you craft yourself contains no data.",
  ],
  "quest.239E5D0B9EB0DC98.title": "&3Fluid Cell",
  "quest.09982FE8CD1BAB6F.title": "&6Deep Space Air",
  "quest.21619170E62020C5.quest_desc": [
    "Refines 10 mB of oil into 5 mB of &aFuel&r and 5 mB of &2Diesel&r at the same time, using 50 FE/t.",
    "",
    "The fluids leave through opposite sides: &aFuel&r from the right and &2Diesel&r from the left. Make sure your pipes are connected to the side you actually need.",
    "",
    "Use &aFuel&r for rockets. &aDiesel&r powers generators and the rover.",
  ],
  "quest.72FC7BAA5713948A.title": "&3Oxygen Propagator",
  "quest.099D3C63BA8A85D9.quest_desc": [
    "Seals food into cans. Outside a breathable room, canned food is the only food you can eat.",
    "",
    "Put food in one slot and an empty can in the other. Each can costs 100 FE and takes 20 ticks per point of nutrition. Hoppers can load and unload the machine from above or below.",
    "",
    "Canning extracts 100 mB of water from the food into the machine's 4000 mB tank. The machine stops when the tank is full, so connect a pipe to drain it.",
  ],
  "quest.115BB85719D018FA.title": "&aPower Bank",
  "quest.2224FF79816EE5A1.quest_desc": [
    "Placing the item raises the whole &73x3&r platform at once, and breaking the center takes the lot apart again.",
    "",
    "Right-click the center with a rocket in hand to stand the ship on it.",
    "",
    "The pad takes two upgrades, both fitted the same way: &6Launch Pad Towers&r and an &3Antenna&r.",
  ],
  "quest.3AE1DC8405E8B7BE.title": "&6The Engineering Station",
  "quest.6EB0B9691B5A733B.quest_desc": [
    "&eStellaris&r uses &aTitanium&r for almost everything. Machines, rocket parts and spacesuit components all need it.",
    "",
    "On Earth, the ore generates from bedrock up to about &ey 60&r, with the best supply in the middle of that range. The Moon has its own deposits below &ey 32&r, but you will need titanium before you can get there.",
    "",
    "&7&oTitanium tools harvest at diamond tier and outlast diamond ones.&r",
  ],
  "quest.11DCEA26B9BA0EC2.title": "&aWater Pump",
  "quest.6D3E46EA2429C2B6.title": "&aSolar Panel",
  "quest.66D1271DB83E2207.quest_desc": [
    "Earth Orbit has gravity 0.5, no breathable air and a temperature of -270 degrees day and night. It is the only place where a space station can be built.",
    "",
    "Stations include an &3Antenna&r, so yours becomes a waypoint as soon as it is built.",
    "",
    "Bring an &6Oxygen Distributor&r to make it breathable and a &3Gravity Manipulator&r to make it easier to move around; neither is included. The &6Star Light Panel&r is the generator that works here.",
  ],
  "quest.427907D696C3BAF6.quest_desc": [
    "The tier 1 tank holds 5000 mB of one fluid at a time. Fill and drain it with pipes, a bucket or a &3Fluid Cell&r.",
    "",
    "A pumpjack extracts oil faster than a refinery can use it. Keep a tank nearby for the surplus, or the pumpjack will soon have nowhere to put more oil.",
  ],
  "quest.09982FE8CD1BAB6F.quest_desc": [
    "Holds 3600 mB of oxygen in the helmet, enough for roughly an hour while standing still in a vacuum. Tier 3 increases that to 6000 mB, or about 100 minutes.",
    "",
    "Modules of the same type replace one another. Install this at the &6Engineering Station&r to upgrade the tank already in the helmet.",
  ],
  "quest.6B965F82617C0CBB.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click to display the oil reserve in the chunk beneath you. The amount appears above the hotbar in mB: &aGreen&r means a rich chunk, &6Orange&r means a small reserve and &cRed&r means none.",
    "",
    "Oil is stored as a hidden chunk reserve rather than a block you can mine. Roughly one chunk in 32 contains between 10 and 50000 mB.",
    "",
    "Each scan uses 1 FE from its 1000 FE battery and 2 durability. Charge it in a &aSolar Panel&r between prospecting trips.",
  ],
  "quest.381894100844F900.quest_desc": [
    "Ordinary farmland does not work off Earth. Without air, crops will not grow or even plant.",
    "",
    "Right-click with dirt to create a dirt farm. Place another within one block, then right-click it with a water bucket; every dirt farm in the surrounding &73x3&r becomes farmland.",
    "",
    "Harvest a grown crop by right-clicking it with a hoe. The drops appear on top, the crop replants itself and the hoe loses one durability.",
    "",
    "&7&oSpace farms use their own growth timer, so a row of them can work in hard vacuum without a nearby distributor.&r",
  ],
  "quest.5AFF8C443EA3B023.quest_desc": [
    "Burns coal or charcoal at 3 FE/t. A piece provides roughly 530 FE, while a coal block provides about 5300 FE. The internal buffer holds 48000 FE.",
    "",
    "It sends power directly into adjacent machines, so a generator and a machine can work side by side without a cable.",
  ],
  "quest.60992E5D06C1A1C7.title": "&cLunar Parasite",
  "task.240601914FC4D949.title": "Any &aCan&r",
  "quest.0E87E42788050B42.title": "&3Electrolyzer",
  "quest.5D751D7FE140340D.title": "&6Oxygen Distributor",
  "quest.7246368D781AF664.quest_desc": [
    "Sets the gravity for the entire chunk it occupies to any value from 0 to 20, using 1 FE/t.",
    "",
    "Jump height, fall speed and fall damage all change with the setting. The same applies to arrows, thrown potions, dropped items, boats, minecarts and primed TNT.",
    "",
    "When unpowered, the chunk returns to its natural gravity: 9.81 on Earth, 1.62 on the Moon and 0.5 in orbit. Multiple manipulators in one chunk average their settings.",
  ],
  "quest.3BD96A538ABED8BB.title": "&bBlue Liquid",
  "quest.4A227306FB8A083A.title": "&3Jet Module",
  "quest.00498F1DCBF49DEB.quest_desc": [
    "Desh Ore generates below y 32 on the Moon and nowhere else. You will need to reach the Moon before you can mine it.",
    "",
    "Desh unlocks equipment titanium cannot provide, including the &3Gravity Manipulator&r, tier 2 and 3 air tanks, better jets, the autopilot and the cargo module.",
  ],
  "quest.353A4A8D9B1F1535.quest_desc": [
    "Adds iron, diamond or netherite-level armor to one suit piece, depending on the module's tier.",
    "",
    "Each module protects only one piece, so a fully protected suit needs four modules.",
  ],
  "quest.72FC7BAA5713948A.quest_desc": [
    "Extends the area a distributor can fill. It needs power, but not its own oxygen supply.",
    "",
    "While powered, it adds its own 3x3 chunks to the allowed area if it is placed inside an area that is already supplied. Air in those chunks does not count against the distributor's 50000-block limit, so propagators can extend a corridor indefinitely.",
    "",
    "An unpowered propagator extends nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.009F038271462E29.title": "&aPipes",
  "quest.108F8B84B41B78DD.title": "&aCable",
  "quest.4972AB9FD8CE627E.title": "&3Rover",
  "quest.00498F1DCBF49DEB.title": "&6Desh",
  "quest.2224FF79816EE5A1.title": "&6Rocket Launch Pad",
  "quest.26652F9A9F60025A.title": "&6The Moon",
  "quest.11DCEA26B9BA0EC2.quest_desc": [
    "Place it &cdirectly on top&r of a water source block. A source beside it or one block lower will not work.",
    "",
    "Each cycle consumes the source below it and stores 1000 mB, then outputs the water from its top face. Connect the pipe there.",
    "",
    "Because the source block is consumed, place it over an infinite water source or it will eventually run dry.",
  ],
  "quest.36F9ED9391019396.quest_desc": [
    "The strongest generator in the mod produces 5 FE/t from its 10000 mB tank. It consumes 1 mB every 5 ticks, or 25 FE per mB.",
    "",
    "Five FE/t will run an oxygen distributor, a propagator and a couple of lights. Larger bases need more generators rather than a higher-tier version.",
  ],
  "quest.0D72E2956CD421AB.quest_desc": [
    "The suit has four pieces, and all four are required. On their own, three of the pieces provide no protection.",
    "",
    "The suit is life support first and armor second. It does not reduce damage until you install a &aDamage Protection&r module, and titanium repairs it.",
    "",
    "The helmet's oxygen module supplies your air, so install one before taking the suit into a vacuum. With oxygen loaded, the suit also lets you breathe underwater.",
    "",
    "Movement uses more air. Sprinting consumes it twice as quickly, and flying with the jets consumes it four times as quickly.",
  ],
  "quest.239E5D0B9EB0DC98.quest_desc": [
    "Stores 3000 mB, or three buckets, in a single item and does not leave an empty container behind. It works with every fluid in the mod.",
    "",
    "Place it in a machine's fluid slot to fill or empty it. While wearing the suit, right-click with it in hand to transfer fuel directly into the chestplate tank and refuel your jets in the field.",
  ],
  "quest.103D7E501EA6144B.title": "&dVaccine",
  "quest.4A227306FB8A083A.quest_desc": [
    "This module goes in the boots and enables flight. Tier 1 uses 8 mB of fuel per second and climbs at 0.35 blocks per tick. Tier 3 uses 3 mB per second and climbs at 0.7, so higher tiers are both faster and more efficient.",
    "",
    "The fuel comes from a diesel or hydrogen tank module on the chestplate, so the boots need one before they can fly. Flying also uses oxygen four times faster than standing still.",
  ],
  "quest.1FD2A6DDDD6FC1DC.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBlender&r has nine input slots, a Blend button and a 6000 FE buffer. It only starts when you press the button, so items left in the grid are safe.",
    "",
    "Input positions and split stacks do not matter. One press processes everything the recipe allows, using more time and energy for larger batches. The result slot is the only limit.",
    "",
    "It also handles every shapeless recipe, giving you a powered alternative to crafting by hand.",
  ],
  "quest.5D751D7FE140340D.quest_desc": [
    "Fills a sealed room with breathable air. Supply power and oxygen, and it spreads air through every block you can walk through.",
    "",
    "The room must meet all three conditions or the distributor empties it:",
    "- &cSealed from the sky&r: one spot with open air above it and everything is gone. A glass roof still counts as sealed.",
    "- &c3x3 chunks&r, measured around the room rather than the machine, over full world height.",
    "- &c50000 blocks&r of air, maximum.",
    "",
    "Air is consumed only by breathing, at 1 mB per creature per update. An empty room uses no oxygen, and a player with a full suit draws from the suit instead.",
  ],
  "quest.29B8507F3604F167.quest_desc": [
    "Registers a launch pad as a landing waypoint, allowing rockets to land there instead of choosing a random location.",
    "",
    "Right-click the center of a finished pad with the antenna. It is placed in the block beneath the center, which must be a soft block. Dirt, sand, air, water, moon sand and moon stone work; stone and building blocks do not.",
    "",
    "Right-click the center with an empty hand to name the waypoint and set it to public or private. Private waypoints are available to players on your &aFriends List&r.",
  ],
  "quest.4FE1E26A7C5491C4.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click to open it. The tablet has four applications. There is a wiki, an SD card reader, a planet list and a page for your personal stats.",
    "",
    "The wiki is the one you will use most. It lists every &eStellaris&r machine, item, creature and rocket part, including the numbers that matter.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click a block to open its page directly. In your inventory, drop an item onto the tablet to open that item's entry.",
  ],
  "quest.7157F03A8C8B2F48.title": "&6Rocket",
  "quest.6EB0B9691B5A733B.title": "&aTitanium",
  "quest.1FB6C3DDFB1760C3.quest_desc": [
    "Generates 1 FE/t at night and nothing during the day. This is the opposite schedule of a &aSolar Panel&r, so one of each can power a base around the clock. It is also the panel that works in orbit.",
    "",
    "The unusual ingredient is &aNovite&r, which does not generate on the Moon. Its deposits are scattered across Earth's surface, so plan a trip home.",
    "",
    "Like the solar panel, it has an item slot that charges at 10 FE/t.",
  ],
  "quest.26652F9A9F60025A.quest_desc": [
    "&dThe Moon&r has a gravity of 1.62, about one-sixth of Earth's. There is no breathable air, and temperatures range from +123 degrees during the day to -233 at night.",
    "",
    "You arrive in a &aLander&r containing you, the rocket and everything in its hold. &cIt explodes on impact&r and can leave a crater, so land away from anything important. An &6Autopilot Module&r makes the landing gentle.",
    "",
    "Remove the rocket from the lander if you want to return home.",
    "",
    "Vacuum deals half a heart of damage per second to anything that breathes. Use a suit with oxygen in its helmet or a sealed room supplied by a distributor.",
  ],
  "quest.48793376ABF73D9D.quest_desc": [
    "A rocket needs three kinds of parts. There is a nose cone for the top, four fins for the bottom corners and an engine underneath.",
    "",
    "The parts do not function on their own. Combine them in the &6Engineering Station&r with titanium for the hull.",
  ],
  "quest.0E87E42788050B42.quest_desc": [
    "Splits water into &aOxygen&r and &aHydrogen&r automatically once supplied. It uses 10 mB/t of water and 50 FE/t to produce 10 mB/t of hydrogen and 5 mB/t of oxygen.",
    "",
    "&aHydrogen&r exits the right side and oxygen exits the left.",
    "",
    "Send the &2Oxygen&r to a distributor to keep a base breathable. &aHydrogen&r can fuel the &bRover's Hydrogen Motor&r.",
  ],
  "quest.6DA7B8D6730BA6E5.title": "&bSD Cards",
  "quest.7908A372EC4E1475.quest_desc": [
    "Insert a filled cell and press Research. Each run takes 30 seconds and empties the cell whether it succeeds or fails.",
    "",
    "There are six stages. For a guaranteed result, they require 1, 100, 200, 300, 400 and 500 parasites respectively.",
    "",
    "Each successful stage rewards an &bSD Card&r containing part of the colony's history. Stage 4 reveals the final ingredient for the cure and unlocks the Vaccine tab. Stage 5 is only the conclusion.",
  ],
  "quest.36F9ED9391019396.title": "&3Diesel Generator",
  "quest.74FDEE7DD7AD56DA.quest_desc": [
    "Place it anywhere in a chunk with an oil reserve and supply power. It extracts 5 mB/t at a cost of 2 FE per mB.",
    "",
    "What comes up is &6Crude Oil&r, the same fluid &eOritech&r pumps out of an oil spring, so either refinery will take it.",
    "",
    "The reserve is finite. Once the chunk runs dry, that pumpjack stops and you will need to find another site.",
    "",
    "&cBreaking it does not return the drill.&r Its other contents are recovered, so choose the location carefully.",
  ],
  "quest.5464B241C8AF9F7A.quest_desc": [
    "&aSilicon&r is used in nearly every electronic part of &eStellaris&r. Cables, pipes, SD cards, the &3Oil Finder&r, the &bAntenna&r and the &6Engineering Station&r all need it.",
    "",
    "Nether quartz is the cheaper input for the &aBlender&r. &aMoon Stone Dust&r works as well, but it takes more energy and is best saved for when you reach the Moon.",
  ],
  "quest.050D217525CEB718.quest_desc": [
    "Unloads a lander after you arrive, so you do not have to climb into the wreck. It empties the rocket and fuel slots first, followed by the rest of the hold.",
    "",
    "Supply power and place it within 5 blocks of the landing site. It moves one stack per second and costs 100 FE per stack.",
    "",
    "It will not search for another lander until all 30 of its own slots are empty, so clear it between flights.",
  ],
  "quest.751C9ACFF61D9B4A.quest_desc": [
    "This module goes in the helmet and supplies the suit's air. Tier 1 holds 1200 mB, enough for about 20 minutes while standing still in a vacuum at 1 mB per second.",
    "",
    "Refill it at an &6Oxygen Distributor&r, or use an oxygen-filled &3Fluid Cell&r while holding it in your hand.",
    "",
    "Tiers 2 and 3 hold 3600 and 6000 mB. Both require desh, so you will need to bring the materials back from the Moon.",
  ],
  "quest.39A64273C8627542.title": "&dPathogen Storage Cell",
  "quest.009F038271462E29.quest_desc": [
    "Pipes move up to 250 mB/t and hold 1000 mB internally. They carry oil, fuel, diesel, water, oxygen and hydrogen, but never energy.",
    "",
    "Use them to move water into an electrolyzer, oxygen into a distributor and oil into a refinery.",
  ],
  "quest.39A64273C8627542.quest_desc": [
    "Stores up to 500 parasites. Right-click while holding it to move every &cParasite&r in your inventory into the cell.",
    "",
    "The &dLaboratory&r empties the cell whether research succeeds or fails, so fill it as much as possible before starting.",
  ],
  "quest.66D1271DB83E2207.title": "&6Earth Orbit",
  "quest.2245CFED83908481.quest_desc": [
    "A small can holds 10 nutrition and a large can holds 20. Neither is a single meal; keep adding food in the &3Vacuumator&r until the can is full.",
    "",
    "To eat one, hold a &aPotion&r in your other hand. A plain water bottle works, and the potion is not consumed while you eat the can.",
    "",
    "Cans come in all 16 dye colors, and you can dye them again later.",
  ],
  "quest.427907D696C3BAF6.title": "&aFluid Tank",
  "quest.0D72E2956CD421AB.title": "&6Space Suit",
  "quest.1FB6C3DDFB1760C3.title": "&6Star Light Panel",
  "quest.099D3C63BA8A85D9.title": "&3Vacuumator",
  "quest.4972AB9FD8CE627E.quest_desc": [
    "A drivable buggy for covering ground without walking. It holds 3000 mB of diesel and uses 2 mB every 20 blocks, so one bucket lasts a long time.",
    "",
    "Modules fit at the &6Engineering Station&r. Cargo adds two more rows, a tank doubles the fuel, speed multiplies the top speed by 1.5, and a hydrogen motor changes what it drinks.",
    "",
    "&cEmpty the tank before switching motors.&r The rover can hold only one kind of fuel at a time.",
  ],
  "quest.5464B241C8AF9F7A.title": "&aSilicon",
  "quest.494E845D8A649A95.title": "&6Star Crawler Boss",
  "quest.3BD96A538ABED8BB.quest_desc": [
    "Blue Liquid forms lakes underground and on the moon. &bBlue Fish&r swim in it, usually in passive schools of three to seven, and flee when attacked.",
    "",
    "Collect the liquid with a bucket and kill the fish for &bBlue Plasma&r. You will need both later. The plasma is used for the &dVaccine&r and the &6Star Light Panel&r.",
  ],
  "quest.494E845D8A649A95.quest_desc": [
    "The &zStar Crawler&r circles a sphere on the surface. It becomes hostile when you come within 48 blocks.",
    "",
    "It has 400 health, 8 armor and 4 armor toughness, and knockback barely affects it. A slow, heavy weapon works better than a fast one.",
    "",
    "Its attacks depend on your distance. At close range it smashes the ground; at longer range it charges. As the fight continues, it gains more attacks, including a leap that brings it down on top of you.",
    "",
    "&7&oThere is no completely safe range, only different risks.&r",
  ],
  "quest.726DF52FC142855E.title": "&aElectric Light",
  "quest.3AE1DC8405E8B7BE.quest_desc": [
    "Build or upgrade everything you fly, drive or wear here. The station has three tabs:",
    "",
    "- &aRocket Station&r: the parts of a rocket, laid out in the shape of a rocket. The finished ship appears in the result slot.",
    "- &aUpgrade Station&r: a rocket, rover or suit piece on the left, a module in the middle, the upgraded item on the right. This is the only way a module ever gets installed.",
    "- &aSpace Station Planner&r: pick a station, fill the grid, take a planned blueprint out.",
  ],
  "quest.41979A3605EC64E2.title": "&6Space Station",
  "quest.2245CFED83908481.title": "&aCans",
  "quest.74FDEE7DD7AD56DA.title": "&3Pumpjack",
  "quest.60992E5D06C1A1C7.quest_desc": [
    "&3Lunar Parasites&r have 8 health and latch onto you instead of attacking normally. They inflict &cInfection&r, which randomly removes one health point while it lasts.",
    "",
    "The damage is random, so an infection is easy to underestimate. It is a nuisance at full health and dangerous when you are already hurt. Milk does not cure it.",
    "",
    "They are common on the Moon and even more numerous underground. They also attack villagers, turning an infected villager into a &cParasite Villager&r.",
    "",
    "You must kill them yourself to obtain a &cParasite&r; there is no other source.",
  ],
  "quest.108F8B84B41B78DD.quest_desc": [
    "Moves energy between machines at up to 20 FE/t. That is enough for four diesel generators before the cable becomes the bottleneck.",
    "",
    "Cables carry energy only. Use &aPipes&r for fluids.",
  ],
  "quest.5AFF8C443EA3B023.title": "&aCoal Generator",
  "quest.7157F03A8C8B2F48.quest_desc": [
    "Assemble it in the &3Rocket Station&r tab by laying out the parts in the shape of a rocket. Put the nose cone on top, titanium through the body, fins at the corners and the engine at the bottom.",
    "",
    "The tank holds 3000 mB of &aFuel&r and every launch burns 1000, so a full ship is three trips. A bucket or a &3Fluid Cell&r adds 1000 at a time.",
    "",
    "Starting the engine begins a 10-second countdown. The rocket then climbs at 0.8 blocks per tick, and the destination screen opens above 400 blocks.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe rocket will not launch if anything is directly above the pad.&r",
  ],
  "quest.2AB8372D4923EB79.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the center of the pad with these in hand to add service arms around it. They do not affect the rocket; they are purely cosmetic.",
    "",
    "Breaking the pad returns the towers as items, so they can be moved without losing them.",
  ],
  "quest.103D7E501EA6144B.quest_desc": [
    "Crafted in the Laboratory's Vaccine tab rather than a crafting grid, and only after research reaches stage 4.",
    "",
    "Right-click to cure your infection and gain permanent immunity. This is the only safe way to approach an &cEvolved Parasite Villager&r, which infects everything within 4 blocks every 1.5 seconds without needing to attack.",
    "",
    "Using it before research is complete only tells you that it is not ready yet.",
  ],
  "quest.6D3E46EA2429C2B6.quest_desc": [
    "Generates 1 FE/t while exposed to sunlight and nothing after dark. The block directly above it must have a clear view of the sky.",
    "",
    "The item slot charges at 10 FE/t, ten times the panel's normal output. Use it to keep an &3Oil Finder&r charged.",
  ],
  "quest.726DF52FC142855E.quest_desc": [
    "A lamp with 16 brightness settings. Setting 0 is off, 1 to 7 are dim and 8 to 15 are bright.",
    "",
    "Brighter settings use power faster. The lowest setting uses 1 FE every 150 ticks, while the highest uses 1 FE every 10 ticks.",
    "",
    "It remembers its brightness when unpowered, so one switched line can turn an entire base on or off.",
  ],
  "quest.41979A3605EC64E2.quest_desc": [
    "A space station is assembled around you in orbit instead of being built block by block.",
    "",
    "Plan it in the Space Station Planner tab of the &6Engineering Station&r. The grid holds the eight required materials and a blank blueprint. Hover over the station to see its requirements, then press the button once to check the grid and again to create the plan.",
    "",
    "Carry the planned blueprint in any rocket cargo slot, choose Earth Orbit and press Build Space Station. The blueprint is consumed as the station is built.",
  ],
}